  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1243 AM CST Wed Nov 4 2026\n\nAs of 12:30 am CST, temperatures across the area are in the upper \n30s to low 40s with winds out of the north between 15 and 20 mph \nwith gusts up to 30 mph. These gusts will be diminishing through the \nnext few hours. This afternoon, winds across northeast SD will gust \nbetween 25 and 30 mph. \n\nPrecipitation continues today across northeast SD. The chance of \nmore than half an inch in additional accumulation is between 45 and \n70% along and east of I-29. Chances farther west up to and around \nthe James River are between 15 and 30%. Due to the recent moisture, \npatchy fog will be possible this morning across portions of central \nSD mainly east of the Missouri River where winds are dying down. \nVisibilities may be reduced to around a mile. Overall, pretty quiet \nweather once we get past today. Temperatures through the end of the \nweek will be right around average before winds shift around to be \nout of the south and raise temperatures to 10-15 degrees above \naverage. There could be some stronger wind gusts Saturday afternoon \nover north central SD, around 25 to 30 mph. Otherwise, winds stay \nrelatively unremarkable through the end of the period.",
